# build-local.env.example — kungfu local build environment config template (mirrors/cache + compile params)
#
# The kungfu repo itself has zero LAN / mirror / machine-parameter coupling: an open-source cloner
# uses the official upstreams and default concurrency out of the box, unaffected by any intranet or
# local config. To accelerate through a LAN cache / CN mirror, or to cap compile concurrency by local
# memory, copy this template to the "user-global" location and fill in your own values (maintainable
# via `kungfu-code config set <KEY> <VALUE>`):
#
#   ./kungfu-code config init        # derive from this template into the user-global location
#   ./kungfu-code config set FNM_NODE_DIST_MIRROR https://...   # or edit directly
#   ./kungfu-code config edit
#
# Location: ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME:-$HOME/.config}/kungfu/build-local.env
# Why user-global instead of in-repo: a git worktree is an independent checkout, so files gitignored
# in the repo do not appear in each worktree; keeping it user-global lets the main repo and all
# worktrees share one copy, and it is naturally outside the repo and open-source safe.
# kungfu-code sources it on startup, then layers the optional repo-root ./build-local.env (already
# gitignored) on top. If nothing is configured, everything uses the official / default upstreams and
# default concurrency. All entries below are optional; uncomment and change them to your values as needed.

# ── Mirrors / cache (per upstream) ──────────────────────────────────────────
# node distribution (fetched by fnm). Official default https://nodejs.org/dist/; CN public mirror or LAN cache example:
# export FNM_NODE_DIST_MIRROR="https://npmmirror.com/mirrors/node/"

# electron binary (fetched by @electron/get, ~120MB zip). Do not set ELECTRON_CUSTOM_DIR.
# export ELECTRON_MIRROR="https://npmmirror.com/mirrors/electron/"

# yarn's own distribution (fetched by corepack). No trailing slash (a trailing slash triggers a //yarn 404).
# export COREPACK_NPM_REGISTRY="https://registry.npmmirror.com"

# pypi simple index (uv installs Python deps). Can also be replaced by index-url in ~/.config/uv/uv.toml.
# export UV_DEFAULT_INDEX="https://mirrors.aliyun.com/pypi/simple/"

# mirror for uv downloading the standalone CPython interpreter (one-time only). Defaults to astral's official upstream.
# export UV_PYTHON_INSTALL_MIRROR="https://YOUR-CACHE-HOST/python-build-standalone/"

# ── Launcher distribution mirrors (one-time bootstrap fetches) ──────────────
# base URL for the prebuilt native kungfu-code launcher (fetched by the kungfu-code shims).
# Defaults to this repo's GitHub releases; a mirror must serve the same path layout:
#   <base>/kungfu-code-v<version>/kungfu-code-<platform>
# export KUNGFU_CODE_DIST_MIRROR="https://YOUR-CACHE-HOST/kungfu-code/"

# base URLs for the prebuilt fnm / uv the native launcher fetches when missing
# (same path layout as the official fnm / uv GitHub release downloads).
# export KUNGFU_FNM_DIST_MIRROR="https://YOUR-CACHE-HOST/fnm/"
# export KUNGFU_UV_DIST_MIRROR="https://YOUR-CACHE-HOST/uv/"

# ── Compile params (cap per machine) ────────────────────────────────────────
# C/C++ parallel compile jobs. kungfu enables -flto + heavy templates, peaking ~2GB per job; on
# many-core machines (e.g. 32 threads) full parallelism will exhaust memory and thrash swap. Rule of
# thumb: jobs ≈ available memory GB / 2. If unset, conan defaults (os.cpu_count).
# export KUNGFU_BUILD_JOBS="12"

# ── Entries not handled by this file — set via their own user-global config (also absent from this repo) ──
#  npm package install registry + private @scope registry / token  →  ~/.npmrc
#    e.g.: registry=http://YOUR-CACHE-HOST:4873/  + @kungfu-tech:registry=...  + _authToken
#  conan remote (e.g. a LAN ConanCenter transparent cache)         →  ~/.conan2/remotes.json
#    e.g.: conan remote add <name> http://YOUR-CACHE-HOST:8083/
